# Build context for the Containerfile. One file for both engines: Docker (BuildKit) reads
# .dockerignore, Podman/Buildah reads .containerignore and falls back to .dockerignore.
#
# Allowlist: everything is excluded, then only what the image needs is let back in. Local-only
# docs, design/, data, secrets and caches can never reach the build context by accident.
*
!backend/pyproject.toml
!backend/uv.lock
!backend/server/agentos
!backend/worker/worker.py
!backend/worker/agentos_worker
!web

# ...minus what never belongs in it, wherever it is.
web/node_modules
web/dist
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/AGENTS.md
**/CLAUDE.md
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
